No, the point *was* to get a version that *runs* nethack. That requires
building it on the machine at some point. And *that* required a *real*
computer. Programmable with libraries, editors, keyboards and proper
utilities such as Make, Gcc, termcap/termlib, Gnu file utils, probably
text utils and ncurses. Alternatively reading Porting and the readme
in the source *may* give other answers. For example it runs under win CE
as well as real computers.

Finally, unless you've actually compiled nethack *without* using nethack wiki,
stay out of such discussions.


